contentText:
The Latin Recording Academy celebrated Monday afternoon (Nov. 9) the contributions of six outstanding performers who have left their mark in Latin music throughout their fruitful careers.

Spanish-Mexican singer Alaska, Cuban-Mexican musician Francisco Céspedes, Mexican singer-songwriter Lila Downs , Brazilian artist Daniela Mercury and Dominican singer-songwriter Chichí Peralta received Lifetime Achievement Awards for their creative contributions of outstanding artistic value to Latin music. Meanwhile, Panamanian hitmaker Omar Alfanno received the Trustees Award, which recognizes individuals who have made significant contributions to Latin music, not necessarily through performance.

